Advanced: run an MCP server behind a recording stdio proxy.

Use it in an agent's MCP server configuration in place of the server command, to record the JSON-RPC traffic between the agent and that server.

Usage: hh mcp-proxy [OPTIONS] -- <COMMAND>...

Arguments:
  <COMMAND>...
          The MCP server command and its arguments, after `--`

Options:
      --session-hint <SESSION_HINT>
          A human-readable hint for a standalone mcp-only session. Accepted for forward compatibility but not yet persisted anywhere (it does not set the session name; use `hh rename`) — it has no visible effect

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  hh mcp-proxy -- uvx my-mcp-server                         record a server's stdio traffic
  hh mcp-proxy --session-hint api-server -- node server.js  same, with a session hint

Docs: https://halfhand.org/docs/mcp-proxy/
